
==========================================================================
  QS_3 dummy-register simulator (n = 3, concrete f_1 = X, f_2 = H, f_3 = Z)
==========================================================================

  Control  (C_1, C_2, C_3) : D ⊗ D ⊗ D    where D = arity-3 datatype
                                              (2 tag qubits each, 6 total)
  Regs     T ⊗ (D_1 ⊗ D_2 ⊗ D_3) : Q ⊗ Q³   (target + 3 dummies, 4 qubits)
  Total    10 qubits.

  R(C_k)  = coherent-controlled SWAP(T, D_{C_k}) via `control` on the
           arity-3 datatype (2 tag qubits → log-depth binary dispatch)
  F       = id_T ⊗ (X on D_1) ⊗ (H on D_2) ⊗ (Z on D_3)  (F² = I)
  round   = R ; (id_D ⊗ F) ; R                          (round² = id)
  qs3_sim = round_1 ; round_2 ; round_3   (with inter-round routing)

  |S_3| = 6 valid permutations; the control register can hold any of
  3³ = 27 basis states, of which 6 are actual permutations.

==========================================================================
  PART 1: Building blocks compile
==========================================================================

R(c)  (log-tree over arity-3 datatype):
  compiled successfully (gate count: 11)

F  (parallel X⊗H⊗Z on dummies):
  compiled successfully (gate count: 3)

round(c) = R ; F ; R:
  compiled successfully (gate count: 25)

qs3_sim  (full three-round pipeline):
  compiled successfully (gate count: 75)

==========================================================================
  PART 2: Structural involutions
==========================================================================

  ✓ R ; R  =  id_{D ⊗ Regs}  (branch-SWAP involution) (fidelity=1.000000)
  ✓ round ; round  =  id  (uses X² = H² = Z² = I on dummies) (fidelity=1.000000)

==========================================================================
  SUMMARY
==========================================================================

  Verifications: 2/2 passed

  QS_3 dummy-register simulator at n = 3 with concrete gates.
  R(C_k) uses log-depth balanced-binary dispatch on the arity-3
  datatype (2 tag qubits). Structural involutions R² = round² = id
  are verified as full unitary equalities on the (D ⊗ Regs) 6-qubit
